 "howMade": "Each set was dressed once on Park's idle frame 0 (face kept pixel-exact), split into slots by region against the bare frame, then carried to every idle/walk/attack frame: rigid parts follow the matching body region, uncovered body pixels are re-shaded from Park's own pixels onto the garment's colour ramp, gloves and boots follow the real hands and legs of each frame, and capes sway with walk/attack. Attack strips (current sprite-gen attack): each set was dressed onto the 8 bare attack frames with PixelLab Pro Flash inpaint (mask = body, face kept pixel-exact, the set's dressed idle 0 in the same image as reference), then split into slots by diffing against the bare frame and by region; pixels where the dressed silhouette came out 1-3 px narrower than the bare body were filled from the neighbouring dressed pixels so no bare body shows through."
}